From 2498d122a9146dffd9348f7a39fdc3d1b2ced11b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:02:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(contour): viewport pick for Start point and Exit
 point

The closed 2D contour's Start point and Exit point groups on the
Lead in / Lead out tab had typed X and Y inputs only (#1938). Add
"Pick start" / "Pick exit" toggle buttons (reading "Stop picking" when
armed) and "Clear start" / "Clear exit" buttons beside them.

Arming unlocks viewport picking off the Geometry tab, routes clicks
through feature_click accepting faces, edges and corners regardless of
toolbar pick mode, refuses fixtures and tilted contours by name, and
writes the clicked model XY into the draft params. Applying or
generating commits the point through EditOperationParams (undoable),
leaving the tab or closing the editor disarms, and pick_ink paints
distinct screen-space markers (diamond for start, X-cross for exit)
at top_z while the Lead tab is open.

Refs #1448
